1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,950
Welcome to VisionCurator, the platform designed to help ML engineers and data
scientists manage and analyze their image datasets. Today, we'll walk through
VisionCurator's Smart Export feature, demonstrating how to create perfectly
balanced datasets for your machine learning models.

2
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:27,074
On the Datasets page, you can see an overview of your uploaded data, including
key metrics like image count, clusters, and identified duplicates or outliers.

3
00:00:27,074 --> 00:00:36,641
Let's explore our 'dogs' dataset. VisionCurator automatically processes your
images, providing a detailed view of your data's structure and content.

4
00:00:36,641 --> 00:00:43,514
You can easily browse through all images, gaining immediate insights into your
dataset's diversity and characteristics.

5
00:00:43,514 --> 00:00:51,594
VisionCurator intelligently organizes your images into meaningful clusters,
helping you understand natural groupings within your data.

6
00:00:51,594 --> 00:01:00,836
Here, we see images grouped into distinct clusters, like Cluster #0 containing
various dark-furred dogs, and Cluster #1 with Shih Tzus.

7
00:01:00,836 --> 00:01:10,913
This clustering capability is crucial for identifying underrepresented classes
or potential biases in your dataset, ensuring a more robust model training
process.

8
00:01:10,913 --> 00:01:20,201
Beyond clusters, VisionCurator also identifies outliers – high-priority edge
cases that are often critical for improving model generalization.

9
00:01:20,201 --> 00:01:29,443
These outliers represent unique or unusual examples that, if included in your
training data, can significantly enhance your model's performance and
robustness.

10
00:01:29,443 --> 00:01:37,384
Now, let's leverage this intelligence with VisionCurator's Smart Export feature,
accessible directly from your dataset view.

11
00:01:37,384 --> 00:01:48,530
Smart Export downloads a perfectly balanced dataset for labeling. It
automatically includes all identified outliers and then divides the remaining
quota equally among all clusters.

12
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:58,514
Simply specify your desired target dataset size, and VisionCurator handles the
complex balancing act, ensuring you get a representative sample every time.

13
00:01:58,514 --> 00:02:09,010
To visualize the underlying data intelligence, let's look at the Embedding
Galaxy. This interactive 3D visualization maps your images based on their
similarity.

14
00:02:09,010 --> 00:02:20,341
Each point represents an image, with colors indicating clusters and specific
markers for outliers or duplicates. This view helps you understand the
distribution that Smart Export optimizes.

15
00:02:20,341 --> 00:02:28,561
You can interactively explore these embeddings, gaining a deeper understanding
of how your data is structured and where the distinct groupings lie.

16
00:02:28,561 --> 00:02:40,914
This visual confirmation reinforces the intelligent sampling performed by Smart
Export, ensuring your exported dataset truly reflects the diversity and nuances
of your full collection.

17
00:02:40,914 --> 00:02:58,561
VisionCurator's Smart Export empowers you to quickly obtain high-quality,
balanced datasets, accelerating your labeling process and improving model
performance. Experience the power of intelligent dataset curation yourself –
visit VisionCurator.com to get started today.